#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064209 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064080 :question/id #uuid "109a6d6e-8e62-5eac-bfa8-7c059399efe8" :question/math-academy-id "e-457" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_0^{1/2}x(1-2x)^5\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-2x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -\\dfrac 1 2 \\,\\textrm d u = \\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x = \\dfrac 1 2 (1-u).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $1/2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}x(1-2x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{0}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}(1-u)\\cdot {u}^{5}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{0}({u}^{5}-{u}^{6})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{(\\frac{1}{6}{u}^{6}-\\frac{1}{7}{u}^{7})|}_{1}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}([0-0]-[\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{7}]) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\left(-\\frac{1}{42}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{168}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "94ad8efa-33ee-5451-b6b9-c99cb81a9ba2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048332 :topic/difficulty 1.7335518935867262 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428117 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen